{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Glibenclamide\", \"id\": \"D005905\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hypotension\", \"id\": \"D007022\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"helodermin\", \"id\": \"C040442\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"helodermin\", \"id\": \"C040442\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"amino acid\", \"id\": \"D000596\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ATP\", \"id\": \"D000255\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"K\", \"id\": \"D011188\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"K\", \"id\": \"D011188\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ATP\", \"id\": \"D000255\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"Helodermin\", \"id\": \"C040442\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hypotension\", \"id\": \"D007022\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"Hypotension\", \"id\": \"D007022\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"glibenclamide\", \"id\": \"D005905\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"levcromakalim\", \"id\": \"D019806\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"helodermin\", \"id\": \"C040442\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hypotension\", \"id\": \"D007022\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"acetylcholine\", \"id\": \"D000109\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ACh\", \"id\": \"D000109\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hypotension\", \"id\": \"D007022\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"helodermin\", \"id\": \"C040442\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hypotension\", \"id\": \"D007022\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"glibenclamide\", \"id\": \"D005905\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"K\", \"id\": \"D011188\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"K\", \"id\": \"D011188\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ATP\", \"id\": \"D000255\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"nitric oxide\", \"id\": \"D009569\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hypotension\", \"id\": \"D007022\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"Glibenclamide","id":"D005905","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"hypotension","id":"D007022","label":"Disease"},{"text":"helodermin","id":"C040442","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"amino acid","id":"D000596","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"ATP","id":"D000255","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"K","id":"D011188","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"levcromakalim","id":"D019806","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"acetylcholine","id":"D000109","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"ACh","id":"D000109","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"nitric oxide","id":"D009569","label":"Chemical"}],"head":"nitric oxide","head_id":"D009569","pairs":[{"head":"Glibenclamide","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"D005905","tail_id":"D007022"},{"head":"helodermin","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"C040442","tail_id":"D007022"},{"head":"amino acid","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"D000596","tail_id":"D007022"},{"head":"ATP","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"D000255","tail_id":"D007022"},{"head":"K","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"D011188","tail_id":"D007022"},{"head":"levcromakalim","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"D019806","tail_id":"D007022"},{"head":"acetylcholine","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"D000109","tail_id":"D007022"},{"head":"nitric oxide","tail":"hypotension","head_id":"D009569","tail_id":"D007022"}],"relations":["C040442 | D007022","D000596 | D007022","D011188 | D007022","D019806 | D007022","D000109 | D007022"],"result":"~","tail":"hypotension","tail_id":"D007022","text":"Glibenclamide-sensitive hypotension produced by helodermin assessed in the rat. The effects of helodermin, a basic 35-amino acid peptide isolated from the venom of a lizard salivary gland, on arterial blood pressure and heart rate were examined in the rat, focusing on the possibility that activation of ATP sensitive K+ (K(ATP)) channels is involved in the responses. The results were also compared with those of vasoactive intestinal polypeptide (VIP). Helodermin produced hypotension in a dose-dependent manner with approximately similar potency and duration to VIP. Hypotension induced by both peptides was significantly attenuated by glibenclamide, which abolished a levcromakalim-produced decrease in arterial blood pressure. Oxyhemoglobin did not affect helodermin-induced hypotension, whereas it shortened the duration of acetylcholine (ACh)-produced hypotension. These findings suggest that helodermin-produced hypotension is partly attributable to the activation of glibenclamide-sensitive K+ channels (K(ATP) channels), which presumably exist on arterial smooth muscle cells. EDRF (endothelium-derived relaxing factor)/nitric oxide does not seem to play an important role in the peptide-produced hypotension.","metrics":{"precision":0.6,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.75,"rel_tp":3,"rel_fp":2,"rel_fn":0}}